Welcome back Tim May.  As always, you have provided us with food
for thought.  Your attempt, though flawed, to compress your
posting was admirable.  It showed us that we must open our minds
to new ideas.  We must boldly experiment.

It is in this spirit that I offer my "Final Solution" to the
problem of list volume, as well as stupid and abusive postings.
My Final Solution combines some previously offered ideas (i.e.,
ratings, peer pressure and a significant cost incentive) with an
exciting element of chance.  Here's how it works:

STEP ONE--Every time you post, each 1K block (or part thereof) of
your message is subjected to a hash function which yields an
integer value between 00 and 99, inclusive.  The longer your
message, the more integer values generated.

STEP TWO--These integers are compared to the first two decimal
digits of the closing Dow Jones Industrial Average next following
your posting.  If none match, you are home free.  However . . .

STEP THREE--If you have a matching integer value, you get to play
the peer review game.  The list administrator calls for a vote of
all list members.  Each list member get to vote "thumbs up" or
"thumbs down."  If the majority of votes are cast "thumbs up,"
you are home free.  However . . .

STEP FOUR--If the majority votes "thumbs down," a contract is put
out on your life and you are killed.  Sure, it sounds harsh, but
hey, nobody is forcing anyone to post, Right?  Now tell me that
wouldn't keep the postings short and polite!

S A N D Y  S A N D F O R T

